I've said this before, but playing Wizards, I just seem to go from one
tight situation to another...

  My most recent wizard is having some mixed fortune: completed
Sokoban and then some, no altars except coaligned at minetown, found
magic lamp early but it was cursed (then an uncursed one in minetown),
found two random BoH lying around, got his wish for +3SDSM and +ID,
then found "Reflection in Sokoban... Minetown was bones, but pretty
useless. Most food rations (even uncursed) I eat turn out to be
rotten. Teleportitis from a leprechaun hall, but no control even after
4-5 tengus. I know this mostly sounds good, but I've had to use just
about every escape item I've found until recently to get out of tricky
situations (hitting magic traps and getting the blind/create monster
effect, etc.).

  Returned to minetown with a bag of tricks hoping to get Magicbane
(lots of sacrificing, but no luck so far)... This is where I screw up
several times. I'm trying to kill a warg in the temple before he runs
